\pard\sb0\sa240\qc\b\f0\fs32\cf1 Q ERRORS\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 PURPOSE\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\b0\f0\fs20\cf0 Checks poetry lines (marked with {\f1\\q}, {\f1\\q1}, {\f1\\q2}) for structural problems that are common formatting or typesetting errors in Bible translation manuscripts.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 PROBLEMS DETECTED\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\b0\f0\fs20 1.\tab{\b Final punctuation followed by text}\emdash a sentence-ending mark (e.g., period) appears in the middle of a poetry line rather than at the end.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 2.\tab{\b Double verse markers}\emdash two {\f1\\v} markers appear on the same poetry line.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 3.\tab{\b Text before a verse marker}\emdash content appears before {\f1\\v} instead of after it.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 4.\tab{\b Hanging word (optional)}\emdash a line ends with non-final punctuation (e.g., a comma) followed by only a single word before the next poetry line.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 HTML REPORT\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\b0\f0\fs20\cf0 In addition to the results list, running the check writes an HTML report ({\f1 QErrorsReport.html}) to the project folder and opens it automatically. Findings are grouped by error type, and each entry shows the full poetry line with the specific problem highlighted in red\emdash including a slightly larger font for a bare final period, which is easy to miss otherwise.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 HOW TO USE\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\b0\f0\fs20 1.\tab Install the Phils Custom (cms) Checks plugin with Install_Phils_tools.exe. Everything comes with the plugin: nothing has to be copied into the cms folder. References in the HTML report can be clicked to show that place in Paratext. The first click makes the browser ask whether to open ParatextGoTo, and Paratext follows only when the text window's scroll group follows other programs.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 2.\tab In Paratext, choose Tools > Phils Custom (cms) Checks..., select this check and click "Run...". In Paratext's check window, choose the books and set the options (Options...) before you click OK.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 3.\tab Review the results; the error type is shown first to make sorting easy.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 OPTIONS\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 FinalPunctuation\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i .!?}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Characters that mark the end of a sentence, used by the final-punctuation check.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 NonFinalPunctuation\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i ,;:}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Characters considered mid-line punctuation, used by the hanging-word check.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 MinCharsBeforePunct\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i 0}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Ignore final punctuation that occurs fewer than this many characters into the line. Useful to skip short lines where punctuation placement is intentional.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 CheckFinalPunct\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i Yes}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Enable or disable the final-punctuation-followed-by-text check.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 CheckDoubleVerse\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i Yes}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Enable or disable the double-verse-marker check.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 CheckTextBeforeVerse\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i Yes}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Enable or disable the text-before-verse-marker check.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 CheckHangingWord\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i No}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Enable or disable the hanging single-word check. Set to Yes to flag poetry lines that end with punctuation followed by exactly one word.\par
}
